1.2.1 Include Sub1
╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌

  First subsection of inclusion. By default this is "indented"
  underneath the parent where the include occurred, so while this is a
  level 1 section in this include file, it was included from a level 2
  section and therefore becomes a subsection of that level 2 section (a
  level 3 section).

◊ 1.2.1.1 Include Sub2

  Sub-subsection of included file. Note that this is the last line, but
  the parent file will continue with this nesting (the include acts as a
  paste, not a sub-parse).

  This is back in the main file, but the paragraph is "continued" from
  where the included file left-off (a level 4 section). However, another
  include statement is relative to the _host_ file include statements,
  so the first level 1 in both the `inc1.org' above and
  the `inc2.org' below will be at level 3, which is 1 level deeper than
  this Subsection 2.

  First line of inc2.


